    "result_text": "The build passes and the acceptance test is green. Here's what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `customerCode` now has the form `<REGION>-<HASH8>` and every value derived from it follows automatically.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 replaced the old sequence-based `nextCustomerCode` (`<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) with `deriveCustomerCode`:\n- **REGION** \u2014 derived from the owner's postcode via a `REGION_POSTCODES` range table (`NSW 2000-2099`, `VIC 3000-3099`, `QLD 4000-4099`), defaulting to `UNKNOWN` when the postcode is absent or out of range.\n- **HASH8** \u2014 first 8 upper-case hex chars (first 4 bytes) of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`, where the telephone is put through `TelephoneNormalizer.toE164` to match the \"normalizedTelephone\" contract. Sequence numbers are gone entirely.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `locality` now reads the `REGION` segment (the part before the first hyphen) straight off the `customerCode`, rather than computing region independently from postcode/city. Removed the now-dead city/postcode region tables, helper, and unused `Map` import.\n\n**Values that ride along automatically** (no logic change needed, they read `customerCode`):\n- `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) and its Luhn `checkDigit` \u2014 now computed over the region-and-hash code.\n- The create audit record in `OwnerRestControllerV1` \u2014 logs the new `customerCode` (confirmed in the run: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. The new `coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` test confirms the code matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`, and I checked that my `%02X`-over-first-4-bytes hashing is byte-identical to the test's own `shaHex` helper.",
